  "note": "马市 (native:guanbei/market; 关北 A): the open yard east of the street — the horse pen with its rails and a dozen steppe ponies, two tethered at the post just sold, the camel pen on the south side, the trader's steelyard on its frame, sacks of fodder, hay, dung and straw everywhere; 卢卡 on his cloth by the pen's south-east corner; the 塞外酒肆's low mud front on the north with its wine flag, the market's earth wall east with the 东门 in it (the camp beyond: 关北 C) and south. Old and used: churned ground, dung, straw blown into the corners, a broken rail.",
